Package: traceAsthma
Type: Package
Title: TRACE-Asthma: A Mechanistic Multi-Omics Asthma Risk Model
Version: 0.3.5
Authors@R: c(
    person("Eskezeia", "Yihunie Dessie",
           email = "estu2003@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(
             Affiliation = paste(
               "Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care, Sleep & Occupational Medicine,",
               "Indiana University School of Medicine"
             )
           ))
    )
Description: Implements the TRACE-Asthma pipeline, an end-to-end framework
    for building and applying a mechanistically informed asthma risk model
    that integrates a multi-trait polygenic risk score (MPRS), a
    methylation-derived expression quantitative trait methylation (eQTM)
    score, and a transcription-factor activity-derived regulatory score
    (TRACE), under the hypothesized architecture
    SNP -> MPRS -> CpG methylation -> eQTM -> TF activity -> TRACE -> Asthma.
    The package provides functions for genotype/methylation/RNA-seq quality
    control, multi-trait polygenic scoring, cis/trans eQTM discovery with
    mediation-based filtering, transcription factor activity inference,
    TRACE score construction with stability selection, structural equation
    modeling of the mediation pathway, nested cross-validated model
    training, external validation, and a clinician-facing prediction
    interface (including an optional Shiny point-of-care app). An adaptive
    pipeline entry point (run_trace_asthma_auto()) inspects whichever data
    modalities a user actually supplies -- e.g. only CpG methylation, gene
    expression, asthma status, age, sex, and ancestry, with no genotype or
    BMI/smoking data -- and builds the best-supported model automatically,
    skipping layers the data does not permit. Nature-family-journal-style
    figure (600 dpi, direct non-generic labeling) and table (fully labeled,
    footnoted) export functions are provided for every major analysis
    output. Heavy domain-specific steps (imputation, VIPER/ARACNe network
    inference, PRS-CSx/SBayesRC scoring) are implemented as documented
    wrapper functions around the relevant external tools/packages so that
    sites can plug in their preferred upstream pipelines while using
    traceAsthma for score construction, mechanistic modeling, prediction,
    and reporting.
